Let $F$ be a complete field with a nontrivial real-valued multiplicative nonarchimedean absolute value. For $r\ge0$, let $T_r(F)=F\langle x_1,\ldots,x_rangle$ be the restricted-series ring [def-trf-restricted-series-presentation]: $f=\sum_{
u\in\mathbf N^r}c_
u x^
u$ has, for every $\epsilon>0$, only finitely many $|c_
u|\ge\epsilon$, and its Gauss norm is $\|f\|=\sup_
u|c_
u|$. Let $B$ be a commutative unital $F$-algebra with a complete norm satisfying $\|1\|=1$, $\|b\|=0\Leftrightarrow b=0$, $\|b+b'\|\le\max(\|b\|,\|b'\|)$, $\|bb'\|\le\|b\|\|b'\|$ and $\|cb\|=|c|\|b\|$ for $c\in F$. For any tuple $b_1,\ldots,b_r\in B$ with $\|b_i\|\le1$, the net of finite partial sums $\sum_{
u\in E}c_
u b_1^{
u_1}\cdots b_r^{
u_r}$, indexed by finite subsets $E\subset\mathbf N^r$, converges. Its limit defines the unique continuous $F$-algebra homomorphism $\operatorname{sub}_b:T_r(F)	o B$ sending $x_i$ to $b_i$. Moreover $\|\operatorname{sub}_b(f)\|\le\|f\|$ for every $f$. For $r=0$ this is the scalar map $F	o B$.
